course: dictionary
lesson: 1412
title: Careful and carefully
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Careful means paying close attention, so you do not make mistakes, break things or get hurt. «Be careful crossing the road» tells you to look, listen and think before you step out.
explain: Careful also means thinking well before you act. «Careful with money» means you spend slowly and think before you buy. In a maths problem, «Be careful to count each one once» is advice: go slowly so you do not miss or double count anything.
explain: Careful work is done slowly and well. «Careful notes let other people check and compare.» Notes that are careful are clear and correct, so someone else can use them. To check a word, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Careful is an adjective: careful, more careful, most careful.
fact: Carefully is an adverb, and it tells you how something is done: «She carefully folded the map.»
fact: Careful means paying close attention so you do not make mistakes, break things or get hurt.
fact: Phrases to remember: be careful, careful with, careful not to, careful of.
fact: «Careful with money» can mean thinking well before you spend, but it can also be a polite way to say someone is stingy, so the sentence around it gives the clue.
exercise: «Be careful crossing the road.» What does careful mean here? | Running as fast as you can | Waiting for a long time | *Paying close attention so you do not get hurt | Singing loudly while you walk
exercise: Which word in «Be careful to count each one once» is advice that tells you to pay attention? | count | each | once | *careful
exercise: «She folded the map carefully.» Which word is the adverb, and what does it mean? | *carefully, meaning with close attention | map, meaning a paper picture of places | folded, meaning bent | she, meaning a girl
test: «Koko's signs need careful tests, because scientists still argue about what she understood.» What does careful show about the tests? | They are very short and quick | *They are done slowly and with close attention | They are only for children | They are noisy and fun
test: «Careful notes let other people check and compare.» Why are careful notes useful? | They are only written in pencil | They are very long and hard to read | They are never looked at again | *They are clear and correct, so others can check them
exam: «Before digital cameras, people took fewer, more careful shots.» What does more careful mean here? | *Taken with more thought and attention, so fewer mistakes | Taken in the dark without a flash | Taken by many people at once | Taken faster and with less thought
